lib-cov
*.seed
*.log
*.csv
*.dat
*.out
*.pid
*.gz

# THE SPEC FIXTURES ARE FIXTURES, whatever they are called. Several of
# the generic patterns above match a file the shared suite reads by
# name -- `conf.csv`, and any `.dat` a future row needs -- and a fresh
# clone missing one would fail that row for the wrong reason: not-found
# where the row is about what the extension MEANS.
!test/spec/files/**

pids
logs
results

npm-debug.log

node_modules
node_modules-*
*~

package-lock.json
yarn.lock
test/coverage.html

coverage
*.off

# Go
*.test
*.cover
go/coverage.out

# Go coverage build artifacts. `make cov-go` builds instrumented binaries
# into go/bin and raw counter files into go/covdata, then removes both --
# but only on success, so a FAILING coverage run leaves them behind and
# the next `git add -A` sweeps 12 MB of binaries into the commit (as one
# did in cc0c2d9).
go/bin/
go/covdata/
go/coverage*.out

# Build artifacts (never commit binaries)
go/aontu
go/bin/
go/covdata/
